course: dictionary
lesson: 368
title: Antihistamine: a medicine for allergies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An antihistamine is a medicine that calms an allergic reaction. An allergy is when your body overreacts to something harmless, like pollen from flowers. Sneezing, itchy eyes and rashes are signs of this reaction.
explain: Your body releases a chemical called histamine when it reacts to things like pollen, pet hair or insect bites. Histamine causes the sneezing and itching. An antihistamine blocks histamine, so the symptoms ease.
explain: «Antihistamine tablets, nasal sprays or eye drops help hay fever.» Hay fever is an allergy to pollen, and the medicine helps it. Antihistamine is a noun here, but it can also be used as an adjective, as in «antihistamine cream».
fact: An antihistamine is a medicine that calms allergic reactions.
fact: «Antihistamines» help with hay fever, itchy eyes and rashes.
fact: Histamine is a chemical the body releases when it reacts to pollen, pet hair or insect bites.
fact: Hay fever is not catching: you cannot catch it from someone else.
fact: Some older antihistamines make you sleepy, so pharmacists can suggest non-drowsy kinds.
exercise: What is an antihistamine? | A pet that helps with allergies | A type of pollen from flowers | *A medicine that calms allergic reactions | A chemical the body makes to fight germs
exercise: «Some older hay fever tablets (antihistamines) reach the brain and cause sleepiness.» What side effect is mentioned? | *Sleepiness | Faster running | Better hearing | Stronger teeth
exercise: What is histamine? | A kind of insect bite | A medicine taken by mouth | *A chemical the body releases when it reacts to things like pollen | A cream for itchy skin
test: Why does an antihistamine help itchy eyes? | It makes the eyes bigger | It cures the pollen itself | *It blocks histamine, the chemical that causes the itch | It stops the body making tears
test: Which of these is true about hay fever? | It can be caught from someone else | It is caused by a broken bone | *It is an allergy, and you cannot catch it from someone else | It is cured by eating sweets
exam: What should you remember when choosing an antihistamine? | Always take the biggest dose you can find | Antihistamines cure every illness | *Some cause sleepiness, so ask a pharmacist for a non-drowsy kind | Antihistamines are a type of sweet
